<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Radar&amp;nbsp;System Design Template&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Simulation Task&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;This workspace is aimed to demonstrate how a Pulse Doppler Radar system works. This PD Radar system works in L band with 1GHz of Center Frequency.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Workspace Description&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;SystemVue has 88 models and 70 templates to cover all advanced radar system designs.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To design your own system, you don&apos;t have to start from scratch.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;SystemVue &lt;STRONG&gt;provides uniform processes &lt;/STRONG&gt;for designing and testing Radar systems using preconfigured simulation templates.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Users can begin by modifying a similar template to their system based on their system spec.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Additionally, your legacy IP in m code or C/C++ code can be imported to SystemVue as SystemVue models, or save it in your own library and use it in conjunction with existing SystemVue models.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In the example, a design for Simulation of a Pulse Doppler Radar system is introduced as a template.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;A PD system in L band with 1&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;GHz of Center Frequency is shown in the example.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;With a LFM source, a Transmitter designing in DSP and RF cross domain (Non-Linear Amp and ADC, DAC), environment scenarios such as RCS for moving target plus clutter as well as noise, Receiver with mixed RF-DSP structure, Signal processing, (pulse compression, MTI and MTD), detector, CFAR and Detection Rate measurement.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Performance measurements include radar transmission signal, target return plus clutter, recovered target through MTI and MTD, signal at the CFAR output.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;A 3D plot is provided to observe the detected target in the radar environments.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Also a performance curve, Detection Rate vs ranges in nautical miles for targets under FFT sizes of 2, 8 and 16 . &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To run the template, please execute the following steps.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1. Open the workspace and observe the main design (design2).&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;a. Sub-Systems: you can see Transmitter, Environments, RF Receiver, Signal processor and measurements.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;By the way, the design supports Cross-Domain architectures in Mod and Demod models.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;If you push into the models you will see it in details.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;b. Key parameters defined using slides: &lt;STRONG&gt;Target Rages &lt;/STRONG&gt;using Nautical Miles, &lt;STRONG&gt;Target Velocity &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;using Radial Velocity, &lt;STRONG&gt;GC Type parameter for Non-Linear Amp in Mod &lt;/STRONG&gt;using&lt;STRONG&gt; &lt;/STRONG&gt;GC_Type, &lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;DAC_NBits parameter&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;for DAC in Mod &lt;/STRONG&gt;using NBits and &lt;STRONG&gt;System Signal to Clutter Ration &lt;/STRONG&gt;using SCR&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;2. Run the simulation by click on the &apos;Run Analysis&apos; button in the first row of Manu bars.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Then you can observe the simulation results.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;a. Tx and Rx Measurements: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;Look the first &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: #333333; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;column&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt; In Figure 1, LFM transmission signal is shown.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 2, the received signal is hidden into the strong Clutter and noise.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 3, through MTI and MTD the pulse is recovered and detected.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 4, the signal at the CFAR output is cleaned up.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;b. Read Parameter Estimation Results.&amp;nbsp;Fidn the Estimated Velocity as well as Estimated Range in the Text Box with light blue color near the slides to specify Key parameters.&amp;nbsp; As can be seen it very closes to its original values specified in the green Text box.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;3. Run Sweep Analysis1 &#x2013; SweepAnalysis3 to get three curves shown the probability of Detection rate VS the ranges in Nautical Miles under different FFT size of signal processor. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;4. Modify Key parameters by using slides to observe the results to know the system works Ok or not.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To create your own system you can modify the template by changing parameters or replace models that are either in the radar library or import your models in the design.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Note:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;In order to create&amp;nbsp;and display doppler figure, equation generate_picture&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;</Text>
